cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "SnowBallSLR: Deterministic, saturation-aware snowballing for systematic literature reviews"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for automated bidirectional citation searching that iterates
  to an explicitly defined saturation point, estimates achieved recall by
  capture-recapture with reported assumption diagnostics, and makes runs
  replayable and auditable against mutating bibliographic APIs: every raw
  response is stored in a content-addressed cache, every emitted artifact is
  hashed into a run manifest, and a verify command re-checks both and classifies
  what the databases changed on refetch.
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/s-matysik/SnowBallSLR"
keywords:
  - systematic review
  - citation searching
  - snowballing
  - capture-recapture
  - reproducibility
  - PRISMA
authors:
